LATENT DISPATCH
Fri Aug 28 · 4 items · ~3 min

PELAGIC 2.5 ADDS EXTENDED REASONING, KEEPS THE PRICE
Pelagic AI's 2.5 release adds an extended-reasoning mode at the same per-token price as the base model, which is the first time a major lab has not charged a premium for thinking. The catch: reasoning tokens are billed as output, and on hard tasks the model thinks a lot. Budget for 3–5x output on anything multi-step. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/pelagic-25

PROMPT CACHING IS BECOMING TABLE STAKES
Argent Systems and Nimbus Inference both shipped prefix caching this week, joining the three labs that already had it. Cached input tokens are running 75–90% cheaper across the board. If your system prompt is 6k tokens and you send it 50,000 times a day, that is real money; we ran the numbers for a typical document pipeline. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/caching-math

A RATE-LIMIT STORY YOU SHOULD READ
A founder wrote up how a background backfill job hit a provider's per-minute token cap, silently fell back to a slower model, and ran for nine days at three times the planned cost before anyone noticed. The fix was boring: a per-job spend ceiling and a daily alert. The post is a good argument for putting cost observability in before the backfill, not after. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/backfill-story

TANAGER-CODER 2 BENCHMARKS
Tanager's coding model lands second on the open agentic-coding leaderboard, first among models you can self-host. 34B, permissive license, and it runs on a single 80GB card at usable speed. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/tanager-coder-2

